                                                                                        <td class="views-field views-field-field-nanu-message-body">NOTICE ADVISORY TO NAVSTAR USERS (NANU) 2025077 NANU TYPE: GENERAL<br />
*** GENERAL MESSAGE TO ALL GPS USERS *** <br />
This is an amendment to NANU 2025075.<br />
<br />
OPERATIONAL NOTICE:<br />
Testing will be starting no earlier than JDAY 339 (05DEC25) using PRN 34 with the third Navigation Technology Satellite (NTS-3) and is planned to continue through June 2027.  GPS users should not attempt to track or use the signals transmitted by NTS-3 since they will not be IS/ICD compliant. <br />
<br />
TECHNICAL INFORMATION:<br />
To mitigate the risk of backward-compatibility issues with GPS user equipment, the NTS-3 PRN34 L1 C/A-code transmissions will include modified Legacy Navigation (LNAV) data comprising alternating 1&#039;s and 0&#039;s in the message content portion of words 3-10 of subframes 1-5 with proper (32,26) Hamming Code parity bits throughout. The most significant bit (MSB) of the six-bit space vehicle (SV) health indication in subframe 1 will be set to 1, indicating &quot;some or all LNAV data are bad&quot;.<br />
*** GENERAL MESSAGE TO ALL GPS USERS ***<br />
POC: CIVILIAN and MILITARY -- AFRL.RV.NTS3@us.af.mil<br />
